303 DISCUSSION AND CONCLUSIONS
304 Our study investigated, through 2 trials, the effects of different rearing substrates
305 on development, waste reduction efficiency, and nutritional composition of BSF
306 larvae.
307 VEGFRU and BRE larvae showed higher weights after 4 days from the beginning of
308 the trial, had lower mortality and needed less time to reach the prepupae stage
309 than FRU and WIN larvae, respectively. Such results were obtained in spite of
310 comparable GE values found in Trial 1 for VEGFRU and FRU and in Trial 2 for WIN
311 and BRE substrates, and can be at least partly ascribed to the higher CP and
